  <prompt>
    Author the Vitest coverage for the Phase-2 client capture surface (Success Criterion 2 — placement
    determinism, client side): (1) the step→operation interceptor (task 020) — a typed edit at an interior
    location emits an operation with the CORRECT `(paraId, runIndex, run-local-offset)` anchor; (2) the
    opaque-atom node (task 021) — atoms render non-editable and preserve document order, and typing inside
    one is a no-op; (3) the rebased operation log (task 022) — rebasing correctness, including the
    rebase-across-concurrent-edits case (edit A then a later edit B earlier in the same paragraph) and the
    op-inside-deleted-content flagging. Test files are colocated under
    `src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/` beside the code they cover (the repo's colocated
    `*.test.ts(x)` convention). MIT ProseMirror base only — NO `@tiptap-pro/*` (NFR-03). Per ADR-038, these
    are behavior tests of real editor transactions — NO `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, DI-registration, or
    ctor-null tests. `build:prod` must be green.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Senior React/TypeScript test engineer fluent in Vitest + ProseMirror/TipTap test harnessing (constructing
    editor states, dispatching transactions, asserting emitted operations). Understands ADR-038 (behavior
    over mocks) and the three capture surfaces under test (020/021/022).
  </role>

  <goal>
    A green Vitest suite covering all three Phase-2 behaviors: correct interior-edit anchors from the
    interceptor; the atom node non-editable + order-preserving with typing a no-op; the rebased op log correct
    across concurrent edits including the deleted-content flag. The suite includes the rebase-across-concurrent
    -edits case and the atom-is-non-editable negative case. `npm run build:prod` for the shared lib is green.
  </goal>

