  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Output the FULL rigor-level declaration (root §8; TEST-MODIFYING override → FULL). Confirm tasks 020/021/022 are complete (the code under test exists). Load ADR-038 + the colocated-test convention.</step>
    <step order="1" name="Interceptor anchor tests">In `stepOperationInterceptor.test.ts`, assert: an interior typed edit emits an op with the correct `(paraId, runIndex, run-local-offset)`; multi-run paragraph maps to the right run; no `{paraId,text}` payload.</step>
    <step order="2" name="Rebased-log tests">In the same file, assert: rebase-across-concurrent-edits (A then earlier B) keeps A's anchor consistent; document-order serialization with a base version; op-inside-deleted-content is flagged, not dropped.</step>
    <step order="3" name="Atom-node tests">In `opaqueAtomNode.test.ts`, assert: fields/SDT render as non-editable atoms in correct order; typing inside an atom is a no-op (negative case); the atom carries its paraId. Checkpoint (context-handoff) per root §5.</step>
    <step order="4" name="Run + build">Run the Vitest suite green for all three behaviors; run `npm run build:prod` (NOT `npm run build`) for the shared lib; confirm no `@tiptap-pro/*`.</step>
    <step order="5" name="Close-out">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md`: set this task's status to ✅. Document any deviation in `projects/spaarkeai-compose-r4/notes/`.</step>
  </steps>

  <ui-tests>
    <ui-test name="Interceptor anchor test is green">
      <steps>Run the interceptor test covering an interior typed edit in a multi-run paragraph.</steps>
      <expected>The test asserts the emitted op's `(paraId, runIndex, run-local-offset)` matches the edit location; suite passes.</expected>
    </ui-test>
    <ui-test name="Rebase-across-concurrent-edits test is green">
      <steps>Run the rebased-log test with edit A then a later edit B earlier in the same paragraph, plus the deleted-content case.</steps>
      <expected>A's anchor is asserted rebased-correct; the deleted-content op is asserted flagged (not dropped); suite passes.</expected>
    </ui-test>
    <ui-test name="Atom-is-non-editable negative test is green">
      <steps>Run the atom test attempting to type into an atom and asserting order.</steps>
      <expected>Typing is asserted a no-op; atoms are asserted non-editable and in document order; suite passes.</expected>
    </ui-test>
    <ui-test name="Dark-mode render (ADR-021)">
      <steps>Include a render assertion mounting the editor with atoms under the Fluent v9 dark theme provider.</steps>
      <expected>Atom placeholders render legibly with theme tokens in dark mode; no hard-coded light colors; assertion passes.</expected>
    </ui-test>
  </ui-tests>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If a test reveals that one of the capture surfaces (020/021/022) does not actually satisfy its FR-03/FR-02 acceptance (e.g. an anchor resolves wrong, or an op is silently dropped), STOP and surface it (root §6) — a failing behavior is a code defect to route back, not a test to weaken.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>No test coverage exists for the step interceptor / opaque-atom node / rebased op log (all new client surface).</existing>
